        "--prompt-en",
        "A photographic dark fantasy scene of an adult fictional woman whose face and hair draw on the supplied appearance reference: a chin-length dark brown bob, separated wispy bangs, broad brown eyes, a soft oval face, and softly glossy pink lips. She is caught inside a dangerous supernatural event, restoring a cracked crystal reliquary in the flooded bell chamber beneath a ruined cathedral. Her attentive, almost tender concentration makes the old object feel like something she has protected for years. She sits on a low, dry stone plinth with both boot soles planted on the same broad dry ledge, her torso leaning slightly toward the work. A fitted, worn charcoal wool dress follows her seated silhouette; its sleeves stop below her elbows and its long skirt gathers naturally around her knees. Damp ends of her bob touch her jaw. Her upper and lower lip edges leave one narrow visible gap; her jaw is only slightly open and her lips conceal her teeth at this viewing angle. Her brow is still, and her gaze is held just past the screw at the escaped root: a quiet hesitation within a skilled repair. The hand-sized crystal reliquary rests securely in a shallow stone recess at the front of the plinth, its transparent body enclosing a coiled black living root. A long fracture interrupts the crystal shell. Her left palm steadies the upper neck, with its fingers curling around the far side; her right thumb and index finger pinch the exposed wings of a small brass clamp screw on the near side of the fracture. Both wrists have clear space, and the screw, fingertips, fracture, and relic remain separately visible. The clamp has begun to draw the two edges together, while a thin silver gap remains open. The actual turning hand, the stabilizing hand, and the crystal object form the photograph's center of attention. Small reflected highlights remain distinct on brass screw wings and the crystal fracture; the subject's surface details stay clean and legible. One escaped root, carrying a faint ash-white internal glow, emerges through that gap, crosses the lip of the plinth and follows an uninterrupted exposed path into the mouth of a fallen bronze bell immediately beside her. It coils around the bell's heavy clapper. The root is drawn taut; the clapper has shifted a few centimeters toward the bell wall, and a narrow wake cuts the otherwise still black floodwater. The nearby bell and the crystal fracture are held in the same readable plane, so the repair and its consequence belong to one event. Pointed stone arches rise from the water behind them, with tide stains crossing carved tomb slabs. Cool overcast daylight from a broken lancet window brushes her face and the crystal seam; a single low votive flame beside the plinth adds a restrained amber reflection to the brass. Her face remains the first human presence, her hands and the relic the next focus, and the root's path leads the eye to the bell. Vertical environmental portrait at the seated woman's eye height, a natural 50 mm perspective, sufficient depth of field for her face, fingers, crystal fracture, and bell clapper to stay legible together. Damp stone, oxidized bronze, uneven wool fibers, small skin variations and the water's imperfect reflections keep the impossible event tactile and photographically credible.",
